## College posting: qualification lines

This is a college or university staff posting. Also return these fields:

- `minimum_qualifications`: every line listed under minimum, required, or
  essential qualifications, one object per line: `{"text": <the line copied
  verbatim>, "type": "experience_length" | "degree" | "technical" |
  "interpersonal" | "other", "years": <number or null>, "domain": <what the
  experience is in, e.g. "web development/programming", or null>,
  "named_terms": [<tools and standards the line names, e.g. "Section 508",
  "ADA", "Cascade CMS">]}`.
- `preferred_qualifications`: the same for preferred or desired lines.
- A line naming both a degree and years of experience is `degree` with `years`
  and `domain` set. Use `experience_length` for lines about years of work.
  Use `technical` for lines about knowing tools, languages, or standards;
  `interpersonal` for working with people, communication, deadlines, or
  priorities; `other` for anything else.
- `allows_substitution`: true when the posting lets education count toward
  experience ("equivalent combination of education and experience", "education
  may substitute", "in lieu of"); copy that phrase into `substitution_phrase`.
- When the posting has no qualification headings, return empty lists.
- Tools and standards in `named_terms` also appear in `keywords`.
